PROGRESSION
{'strand': 'inq', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-narrow-and-plan', 'standard': 'AASL.I.B.2; ~AASL.I.A.1', 'assumes': 'g3-research-questions', 'hands_on': 'g5-research-or-guess; g5-search-log-look-back', 'model_in': 'research-cycle', 'model_out': 'research-cycle', 'words': 'narrow; subtopic; plan; step', 'cross_subject': 'social-studies:ss4-canada-mexico-research (host task: a research project on a neighboring country); ela:e4-research (short research projects on different aspects of a topic)', 'notes': 'Students pick an interesting part of a broad topic, write two or three questions about it with a predicted answer, and make a research plan: what they still need to know, which sources they will try and in what order. Checked alone in grade 4: a plan for a new topic whose sources fit its questions. Owned here.'}
{'strand': 'exp', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-own-question', 'standard': 'AASL.V.A.3; ~AASL.V.C.1', 'assumes': 'g3-research-questions', 'hands_on': 'g5-research-or-guess', 'model_in': 'research-cycle', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'curious; choose; explore', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'A short free-choice inquiry: each student picks a question of their own from a neutral list or their own wonder (how do bees make honey?), researches it just to learn, names who the sheet is for before choosing its form, and makes a one-page "I found out" sheet with a source list. Checked alone in grade 4: the question is the student\'s own and the sheet answers it. Teacher note: questions stay on neutral ground in K to 5; the teacher steers a sensitive choice to a nearby neutral one privately.'}
{'strand': 'cur', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-search-more-kinds', 'standard': 'AASL.IV.B.1; ~AASL.VI.A.1', 'assumes': 'g3-key-words; g3-safe-searching', 'hands_on': 'g5-search-revise', 'model_in': 'search-plan', 'model_out': 'search-plan', 'words': 'catalog; encyclopedia; website; compare', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Students search the catalog, a print or online children's encyclopedia and a teacher-chosen or invented results page for the same question with the same key words, and record what each kind gave. Inside a book they use the contents, index and glossary to reach the part that answers. Checked alone in grade 4: a search plan that uses at least two kinds of source and says what each was good for. Owned here; later grades refine the search."}
{'strand': 'cur', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-primary-secondary', 'standard': '~AASL.IV.B.3; ~AASL.IV.A.3', 'assumes': 'g3-source-kinds-and-makers', 'hands_on': 'g5-choose-sources; g5-first-lateral-check', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'firsthand; secondhand; persuade; advertisement', 'cross_subject': 'social-studies:ss4-primary-source (using primary sources); ela:e4-firsthand-secondhand (comparing firsthand and secondhand accounts)', 'notes': "Students compare a primary and a secondary source the teacher chose on the same topic, say what each can tell that the other cannot, and sort invented pages by purpose (inform, persuade, sell, entertain), finding the ad on a page. Grade 4 adds purpose sorting and the ad to grade 3's kinds."}
{'strand': 'cur', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-evidence-notes', 'standard': 'AASL.I.B.1; AASL.IV.B.4', 'assumes': 'g3-notes-in-boxes', 'hands_on': 'g5-evidence-notes', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'evidence; answer; own words; related', 'cross_subject': 'ela:e4-evidence-inference (referring to details and examples in a text); science:s4-energy-resources (host task: information about energy resources); ela:e4-research (taking notes and sorting them into categories the student makes)', 'notes': 'Students read a source with their research question beside them and note only the facts that answer it, in their own words, marking what is opinion as opinion, crossing out "interesting but not an answer" facts. Notes go into categories the student makes and can explain. Checked alone in grade 4: notes on a new text that keep the answers (I.B.1), sorted into the student\'s own labeled boxes with the plan said (IV.B.4). Owns both.'}
{'strand': 'eng', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-honest-use', 'standard': 'AASL.VI.A.2; ~AASL.VI.B.2', 'assumes': 'g3-source-list', 'hands_on': 'g5-bibliography', 'model_in': 'citation', 'model_out': 'citation', 'words': 'honest; copy; own words; credit', 'cross_subject': 'ela:e4-research (taking notes and giving a list of sources)', 'notes': 'Students explain in their own words what honest use means: putting an idea in your own words, using a few exact words in quotation marks with the source, saying where it came from, and why a maker cares; they sort cases into honest and not yet honest, and fix the second kind. Checked alone in grade 4. Teacher note: honest use is taught without shaming; a student who copied is helped to put it in their own words and cite, never named in front of the class.'}
{'strand': 'inq', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-revise-from-advice', 'standard': 'AASL.I.C.3; ~AASL.I.C.2', 'assumes': 'g3-make-product; g3-gallery-feedback', 'hands_on': 'g5-share-real-audience', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'revise; advice; change', 'cross_subject': 'ela:e4-writing-process (revising with guidance from peers and adults)', 'notes': 'After a feedback round, students choose which advice to use on their research product, make the changes and keep a short change log (advice, what I changed, or why I kept it). Checked alone in grade 4: a revised product with a log that matches the changes. Owned here.'}
{'strand': 'exp', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-class-survey', 'standard': 'AASL.V.C.2; ~AASL.III.D.1', 'assumes': 'g3-research-team', 'hands_on': 'g5-group-inquiry', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'survey; observe; tally; plan', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "When no source holds the answer, a group works out a new way to find out: a class survey on a neutral question (which of three read-aloud books the class wants to hear again) or an observation plan (birds at a feeder for a week), writes the steps, collects and tallies. Checked alone in grade 4: each student explains the group's plan and why it answers the question. Teacher note: survey rules, APPROACH Sensitive ground 8."}
{'strand': 'inc', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'g4-asking-others', 'standard': 'AASL.II.D.2; ~AASL.II.A.1', 'assumes': 'g3-research-team', 'hands_on': 'g5-group-inquiry', 'model_in': '', 'model_out': '', 'words': 'interview; viewpoint; listen; record', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Students plan three open questions to ask a classmate or a school adult how they see the research topic (what they know, what they would want to find out), ask them, listen without arguing, and record the answer. Checked alone in grade 4: the questions are open and the record matches what was said. Teacher note: interview rules, APPROACH Sensitive ground 8.'}
